# Operational documents are not source. The server pentest report in particular is a map of the access model,
# the firewall and the deploy account — publishing your own pentest is publishing the attacker's homework. The
# ceremony runbooks and funding envelopes describe procedures rather than secrets, but they belong with the
# operator, not on a public page. Moved to artifacts/local/ops-archive/ on 2026-08-20; these two are also
# GENERATED by scripts that write into artifacts/, so they are named here or the next run re-adds them.
artifacts/m20t_testnet_funding_readiness.json
artifacts/buybackburn_funding_envelope_m19h.json
artifacts/M20T_TESTNET_FUNDING_*
artifacts/SERVER_PENTEST_REPORT_*
artifacts/*CEREMONY_RUNBOOK*
artifacts/*REGEN_RUNBOOK*

# The operator console (tools/admin) is LOCAL ONLY — it stays on the owner's machines and out of the public
# repository (owner, 2026-08-21: nothing secret in it, but not for showing). Its own gate lives beside it and runs
# through vitest.admin.config.ts (`npm run admin:test`) on a machine that has the folder — never through the
# canonical `npm test`, whose file count is recorded as release evidence and compared with tests/ on every machine.
tools/admin/

# The design working copy lives OUTSIDE the repo (C:\plathodesign) and must never be committed — even if copied in.
plathodesign/
/plathodesign/

# clean-18 contract lane - local-only while in development [OWNER 2026-08-27: a separate folder, not pushed
# yet; hotfixes to the live app must never depend on or collide with it]. The canonical test suite includes
# tests/** only, so nothing here can change the release evidence either.
contracts18/
